{"name":"Dandelion Wine","hex":"#fcf2b9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dandelion wine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wine made from dandelion flowers and usually other ingredients, including citrus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dandelion_wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dandelion Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Dandelion Wine is a 1957 novel by American writer Ray Bradbury, set in the summer of 1928 in the fictional town of Green Town, Illinois, based upon Bradbury's childhood home of Waukegan, Illinois. The first novel in his Green Town Trilogy, the book developed from the short story \"Dandelion Wine\", which appeared in the June 1953 issue of Gourmet magazine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Dandelion_Wine_%281957%29_1st_edition_front_cover.jpg/330px-Dandelion_Wine_%281957%29_1st_edition_front_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dandelion_Wine","wikidata":"Q1810196"},{"title":"Dandelion Wine (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Dandelion Wine are a musical trio based in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia. The band combines medieval and Middle Eastern instruments with electronic beats, analogue synths, female vocals and swirling guitars. Their music incorporates elements of ethereal, medieval, world music, dream pop, electronica and darkwave."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/M%C4%97nuo_Juodaragio_XXI_Dandelion_Wine_%282%29.jpg/330px-M%C4%97nuo_Juodaragio_XXI_Dandelion_Wine_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dandelion_Wine_(band)","wikidata":"Q5215690"},{"title":"Fruit wine","blocks":[{"text":"Fruit wines are fermented alcoholic beverages made from a variety of base ingredients ; they may also have additional flavors taken from fruits, flowers, and herbs. This definition is sometimes broadened to include any alcoholic fermented beverage except beer. For historical reasons, cider and perry are also excluded from the definition of fruit wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/%D5%86%D5%BC%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%A3%D5%AB%D5%B6%D5%AB.jpg/330px-%D5%86%D5%BC%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%A3%D5%AB%D5%B6%D5%AB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_wine","wikidata":"Q633625"},{"title":"Taraxacum","blocks":[{"text":"Taraxacum is a genus of flowering plants in the family Asteraceae which consists of species commonly known as dandelions. The scientific and hobby study of the genus is known as taraxacology. The genus has a near-cosmopolitan distribution, absent only from tropical and polar areas. Two of the most common species worldwide, T. officinale and T. erythrospermum, are European species introduced into North America, where they are non native. Dandelions thrive in temperate regions and can be found in yards, gardens, sides of roads, among crops, and in many other habitats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/DandelionFlower.jpg/330px-DandelionFlower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taraxacum","wikidata":"Q30024"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Elderberryfruit5081.JPG/250px-Elderberryfruit5081.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Elderberryfruit5081.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Elderberryfruit5081.JPG/250px-Elderberryfruit5081.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Elderberries, a common fruit wine ingredient.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElderberryfruit5081.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Pineapple_wine_bottle.jpg/500px-Pineapple_wine_bottle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Pineapple_wine_bottle.jpg/500px-Pineapple_wine_bottle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bottle of pineapple wine from Dominican Republic","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APineapple_wine_bottle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/PikiWiki_Israel_46764_Entertainment.jpg/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_46764_Entertainment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/PikiWiki_Israel_46764_Entertainment.jpg/1280px-PikiWiki_Israel_46764_Entertainment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/PikiWiki_Israel_46764_Entertainment.jpg/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_46764_Entertainment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pomegranate wine in Israel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APikiWiki_Israel_46764_Entertainment.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/TaraxacumOfficinaleSeed.JPG/500px-TaraxacumOfficinaleSeed.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/TaraxacumOfficinaleSeed.JPG/1280px-TaraxacumOfficinaleSeed.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/TaraxacumOfficinaleSeed.JPG/500px-TaraxacumOfficinaleSeed.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaraxacumOfficinale